      "bluetooth": "v4.2 BR/EDR + BLE",
      "adc": "2x 12-bit SAR (18 channels)",
      "dac": "2x 8-bit",
      "flash size": "typically 4MB on WROOM-32",
      "operating": "3.0V to 3.6V"
    }
  },
  "typical_application": "Wi-Fi/BLE IoT nodes, sensor hubs, web servers. Power the 3V3 pin from a regulator able to supply ~500mA peaks (Wi-Fi TX bursts). Use ADC1 pins for analog while Wi-Fi is on, since ADC2 is shared with the radio.",
  "gotchas": [
    "GPIO6-11 are bonded to the internal SPI flash; using them bricks code execution",
    "GPIO34/35/36/39 are INPUT ONLY, no pullups and no output",
    "ADC2 cannot be read while Wi-Fi is active; use ADC1 (GPIO32-39) for analog when networking",
    "strapping pins (0, 2, 5, 12, 15) set boot mode; external loads on them can stop the board from booting. GPIO12 must be LOW at boot or the flash voltage is wrong",
    "the 3.3V regulator on cheap dev boards often cannot supply Wi-Fi current peaks, causing brownout resets",
    "GPIO0 low at reset enters the serial bootloader (how the auto-program circuit flashes it)"
  ],
